26.m:
Lomaharṣaṇa said:
Long ago the sages asked my teacher this very question;
I shall tell you that which you ask, O best of the twice-born.

The sages said:
O blessed one, we wish to hear of the land of action on the surface of the earth;
you ought to tell us, O lord of gods, of the rarely attained holy place of liberation.

27.m:
The sages said:
Since it was said by you that action nowhere else yields merit
or leads to evil, O best of the gods, except in Bhārata;

Brahmā said:
Listen, O twice-born, to the realm of Bhārata in its ninefold division;
they should be understood as separated by the ocean, yet equal to one another:
